WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.940
Solo: A Star Wars Story isn't set to fly into
cinemas until May 25th, but a handful of lucky

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:10.570
movie lovers got to board the Millennium Falcon
ahead of time for a journey to a galaxy far,

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:11.670
far away.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:16.199
The latest entry in the sprawling Star Wars
franchise, Solo had its world premiere May

00:00:16.199 --> 00:00:20.520
10th in Los Angeles, and those who attended
the star-studded event have taken to social

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.560
media to spill their spoiler-free thoughts
on the Ron Howard-directed standalone.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.670
IndieWire film editor Kate Erbland writes
...

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.349
"It takes a bit for it to find its feet and
for Alden Ehrenreich to turn on enough charm

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:34.430
to make you forget he’s not [Harrison Ford].

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:38.600
But once it kicks into its hey-let’s-make-a-crew
and yes-also-do-a-heist stuff, it totally

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.600
flies."

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.420
Erland also gushed about Donald Glover's "delightful"
performance as young Lando Calrissian and

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.150
praised Phoebe Waller-Bridge, who voices Lando's
droid companion, L3-37

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:54.100
Yahoo Entertainment senior correspondent Kevin
Polowy felt much the same, writing that while

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.789
Ehrenreich's performance is excellent, L3
is the real scene-stealer.

00:00:57.789 --> 00:01:02.770
Polowy also noted how the film's overall tone,
which is lighter in comparison to its mostly

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:05.590
serious predecessors, works to its advantage.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:08.350
"Solo: A Star Wars Story is reaaaaalllly good.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.350
Fun as hell.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:13.270
It's a straight intergalactic heist movie,
kind of refreshing to see a Star Wars movie

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.170
without a Death Star or the rebellion's fate
at stake.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.899
Alden Ehrenreich is super impressive as Han,
but L3 might be my favorite new character."

00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:25.560
Angie J. Han of Mashable echoed those sentiments
while also giving a sweet shoutout to Thandie

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.560
Newton's Val:

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.459
"Alden Ehrenreich is the real deal, Thandie
Newton is who I want to be when I grow up,

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:34.139
and Phoebe Waller-Bridge's L3… well we'll
talk about that later."

00:01:34.139 --> 00:01:38.639
Mike Ryan, senior entertainment writer at
Uproxx, called out the first half of the film

00:01:38.639 --> 00:01:42.609
as "hit and miss clunky," but says once the
heist plot is in full swing, it's "a whole

00:01:42.609 --> 00:01:43.609
lot of fun."

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:48.350
Ryan also calls Donald Glover's Lando "legit
fantastic" and, in perhaps the most intriguing

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.489
reveal about the film so far, says ...

00:01:50.489 --> 00:01:54.299
"It's not really hiding the fact it's setting
up more Han Solo movies."

00:01:54.299 --> 00:01:59.990
CinemaBlend's Eric Eisenberg was even less
enthused, sharing one of the few not-quite-negative-but-not-positive-either

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:01.430
reactions thus far.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.630
"Solo: A Star Wars Story is … fine.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:08.369
It's slow to find its footing, but picks up
in the second act, and it's definitely fun.

00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:12.670
Has the occasional prequel problem answering
questions I didn't need answers to, but also

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.490
some fun references.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.250
Overall I liked it, didn't love it."

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.319
Off that lukewarm response to Solo, there's
a flurry of wonderful words from Slashfilm

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:25.129
head Peter Sciretta, who praised the film
for its portrayal of young Han Solo and for

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:26.350
its unexpected twists:

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:28.180
"Solo was a blast.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.620
[Screenwriters Jonathan and Lawrence Kasdan
nail the character of Han Solo.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.069
Yes, the story is a series of expected events
[...] but none of them happen as expected.

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:39.950
Stay away from spoilers, big Marvel-level
s--- that will make you wonder where Lucasfilm

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.010
is headed next."

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.879
Sciretta concludes that the finished product
more than makes up for the production troubles

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:49.340
the project faced — including the firing
of original directors Phil Lord and Christopher

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.340
Miller.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.980
"Regardless of any of the production problems,
the finished film is going to make most fans

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:54.980
happy."

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:58.310
Fans can decide for themselves how Solo: A
Star Wars Story stacks up when the film hits

00:02:58.310 --> 00:02:59.900
theaters on May 25th.

